{
 "about": "Per-class arbitration of the F kernel's VRR side between the ket cascade (hgp.vrr, [Fock] eqs 25-26) and the electron-transfer relation (hgp.etr, #354), from src/felizjueves/f_levers/etr.py. Rule: per class, score the ket cascade (hgp.vrr.build) and the ETR (hgp.etr.build) on (peak, x): peak = hgp.vrr.vrr_peak, the statement-order live model (#350's), x = hgp.cost's K^4 FLOPs per primitive quartet (cost / etr_cost); the ETR when its (peak, x) is lexicographically lower, else the cascade (a tie on both keeps the literal kernel); then THE ACCURACY GATE: the ETR ships only on a class whose interpreted ETR F is recorded within the F tolerance (ACCURACY, ACCURACY_TOL), else the cascade; OVERRIDES wins. The cost half is a model's opinion, not a measurement: a measured selector (#362) may override it. peak_margin and x_margin are cascade minus ETR (positive: the ETR saves); opinions_agree is whether the two point the same way; rule is the model's choice. accuracy is the ETR forced, worst error / scale on H2O/cc-pVDZ, launch_f's plan at tau = 0, n = 1 (test_fock_ondevice.py's PART1): every launch of the class, the kernel the ETR forced (`forced(ETR)`), interpreted, against ao.fock's sweep restricted to the quartets those launches meet, worst |F - G| / scale_G (scale_G: the sweep on |D| with ao.eri's absolute-value twin); gate is admitted when it is within 1e-13, refused when not, unverified with no record (L > 4, milestone 13's cap); choice ships the ETR only where rule says etr and gate is admitted. Model numbers only, calibrated against nothing: the compiler's registers and spills for both recurrences are printed by test/test_f_lever_etr_device.py, not stored here.",
